1
00:00:00,060 --> 00:00:02,020
- Oh, hey, Leonard.
- Good afternoon, Penny.

2
00:00:02,187 --> 00:00:04,567
(Leonard:)So, hi, hey. Uh...

3
00:00:05,691 --> 00:00:07,691
(Leonard:)I was wondering
if you had plans for dinner.

4
00:00:07,860 --> 00:00:09,240
Uh, you mean, dinner tonight?

5
00:00:10,738 --> 00:00:13,318
(Leonard:)There is an inherent ambiguity
in the word "dinner."

6
00:00:13,490 --> 00:00:16,330
(Leonard:)Technically,
it refers to the largest meal of the day.

7
00:00:16,493 --> 00:00:19,033
(Leonard:)So to clarify here,
by dinner, I mean supper.

8
00:00:19,413 --> 00:00:21,203
- Supper?
- Or dinner, you know.

9
00:00:22,499 --> 00:00:25,129
I was thinking 6:30 if you can go,
or a different time.

10
00:00:25,294 --> 00:00:26,464
Uh, 6:30 is great.

11
00:00:26,628 --> 00:00:28,088
(Leonard:)Really?

12
00:00:30,007 --> 00:00:32,217
(Penny:)- Great.
- Yeah, I like hanging out with you guys.

13
00:00:32,384 --> 00:00:33,424
(Leonard:)Us guys?

14
00:00:33,594 --> 00:00:36,474
Oh, you know, Sheldon, Howard, Raj.
Who all is coming?

15
00:00:37,514 --> 00:00:38,934
(Leonard:)They...

16
00:00:39,767 --> 00:00:42,057
(Leonard:)...might all be there.

17
00:00:43,187 --> 00:00:45,897
(Leonard:)Or a subset of them might be there.

18
00:00:46,064 --> 00:00:48,354
(Leonard:)Algebraically speaking,
there are too many unknowns.

19
00:00:48,525 --> 00:00:50,525
(Leonard:)For example,
Sheldon had Quizno's for lunch.

20
00:00:50,694 --> 00:00:53,234
(Leonard:)Sometimes he finds that filling,
other times he doesn't.

21
00:00:53,405 --> 00:00:58,025
It's no fault of Quizno's.
They have a varied menu.

